"""Outlined wordmark glyph paths — BRAND06 part 2.

The lockup type is committed as vector paths so the wordmark no longer depends on a font at render
OR build time (build.py stays stdlib-only + deterministic). This is the "outline once and commit"
ruling; the same pattern as src/monogram.svg ("TS as paths").

RECIPE — to redo when a product name or tagline changes (a deliberate MANUAL step, not automated):
  font   Inter 4.1 (github.com/rsms/inter, release v4.1), static TTFs:
           Inter-Bold.ttf    sha256 288316099b1e0a47a4716d159098005eef7c0066921f34e3200393dbdb01947f
                             -> the NAME ("Trouba" + tail), 88px, weight 700
           Inter-Medium.ttf  sha256 97ad806f526e41546d46365bb3a393145f75b7b1568913db74549ad8b8dba872
                             -> the TAGLINE, 25px, weight 500, letter-spacing 3.4
  layout name at x=40 y=118; tagline at x=44 y=168; viewBox 0 0 900 220 (as WORDMARK_TEMPLATE)
  tool   Inkscape 1.4.4, headless:
           inkscape in.svg --actions="select-all;object-to-path;export-plain-svg;export-filename:out.svg;export-do"
         each segment carried a sentinel fill so the output paths split cleanly into name/tail/tagline.
  verify rsvg-convert render of the outlined SVG is pixel-identical to the former <text> render with
         Inter installed (ImageMagick compare -fuzz 25% -> 0 differing pixels).
  source the exact strings are build.py's WORDMARKS dict; keep them in sync if you re-outline.

The wordmark text is now FROZEN: changing a name/tagline means re-outlining by this recipe.
"Trouba" is identical for all four marks (same word/font/size/position), so it is stored ONCE.
"""

